\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. All praise to Him who dwells in bliss,
\par Who made both day and night,
\par Whose throne is darkness in the abyss
\par Of uncreated light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Each thought and deed His piercing eyes
\par WIth strictest search survey;
\par The deepest shades no more disguise
\par Than the full blaze of day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Whom Thou dost guard, O King of kings,
\par No evil shall molest;
\par Under the shadow of Thy wings
\par Shall they securely rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thy angels shall around their beds
\par Their constant stations keep;
\par Thy faith and truth shall shield their heads
\par For Thou dost never sleep.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. May we, with calm and sweet repose,
\par And heavenly thoughts refreshed,
\par Our eyelids with the morn's unclose,
\par And bless the Ever- blessed.
\par                         Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
